# tally 2.2.1 S-232 (L §5.19 "each observation that stands (§4.6)"; E §3.1 step 9: LOAD-COVERS "on the rows that
# stand, per world and cut class"; P19):
# late narrows stmt, mv stacks on it: both refused, mv with late's message (OPERATIONS §2.1).
# tally 2.2's refcore: ok (T's held fixture/reviews/stacked-covers).
=== options check exit=1
=== base.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place shop: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
input bank: observed

version open
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..2026-04-30
  known 2026-01-02
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-02-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to shop amount 50.00 PLN) "a"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-03-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to shop amount 20.00 PLN) "b"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-04-30)
=== late.tally
scenario late over mv
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version late_v
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-04
  replace bank[r2] = none "gone"

ask q_late: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) in late
=== mv.tally
scenario mv over t
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version mv_v
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-03
  moves stmt to 2026-01-01..2026-02-28

ask q_mv: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) in mv
=== expect
scenario late: refused: LOAD-COVERS observation bank[r2] of konto is dated outside the span stmt covers (base.tally:25)
scenario mv: refused: LOAD-COVERS observation bank[r2] of konto is dated outside the span stmt covers (base.tally:25)
